---
/**
 * About — who runs this site and how it decides what is true.
 *
 * Two reasons this page exists:
 *   1. AdSense readiness (ADS-UX-05 / ADS-PUB-05): a publisher that will not say
 *      who it is fails both the trust-page and the misleading-representation
 *      checks. Before this, the only statement of identity on the whole site was
 *      the footer line "Independent reference. Not affiliated with OpenRouter…".
 *   2. The site's own editorial rule is worth stating out loud: catalogue fields
 *      are facts with a date, everything else is a claim with a source, and the
 *      two never share a surface. A reader who knows that can calibrate the rest.
 *
 * See docs/audits/adsense-readiness-2026-09-18.md for the audit that asked for it.
 */
import System from "../../layouts/System.astro";
import JsonLd from "../../components/JsonLd.astro";
import { breadcrumbSchema, SITE, SITE_NAME } from "../../lib/schema";

const title = "About Hunter Alpha Hub";
const description =
  "Who runs this OpenRouter reference, how model facts are verified and dated, how claims are labelled, and how to report a correction.";
const canonical = `${SITE}/about`;
---
<System title={`${title} | ${SITE_NAME}`} description={description} canonical={canonical} lang="en">
  <JsonLd
    slot="head"
    data={breadcrumbSchema([
      { name: "Home", url: SITE },
      { name: "About", url: canonical },
    ])}
  />

  <p class="kicker">About</p>
  <h1 class="display">Who runs this site, and how it decides what is true</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    Hunter Alpha Hub is an independent reference for models on OpenRouter, run by a small independent
    team. It is not affiliated with OpenRouter, with any model provider, or with any other company
    named on the site.
  </p>

  <h2>What this site is for</h2>
  <p style="max-width: var(--measure); color: var(--text-muted);">
    Two jobs. First, a durable reference for picking a model: pricing, context window, modality and the
    workloads each model actually suits, read from the public OpenRouter catalogue rather than copied
    from a press release. Second, a record of the anonymous Alpha releases — what each one claimed,
    what it turned out to be, and when its free window closed.
  </p>
  <p style="max-width: var(--measure); color: var(--text-muted);">
    The second job has a short shelf life by design: a codename is a marketing device with an expiry
    date. The first one is why the site keeps going after each reveal.
  </p>

  <h2>How we decide what to publish</h2>
  <div class="grid-cards">
    <article class="card">
      <p class="card-kicker">Rule 1</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">Facts are read, not remembered</h3>
      <p class="card-body">
        Prices, context windows and modalities come from the public catalogue and are re-checked by a
        scheduled drift check. Every data page states the date its numbers were verified.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="card-kicker">Rule 2</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">Claims are labelled</h3>
      <p class="card-body">
        Community findings, vendor statements and our own inferences are marked as claims with their
        source. A claim never appears in a field that is otherwise a verified fact.
      </p>
    </article>
    <article class="card">
      <p class="card-kicker">Rule 3</p>
      <h3 class="card-title">Uncertainty is printed</h3>
      <p class="card-body">
        Where something could not be verified, the page says so instead of filling the gap with a
        plausible number. "Unknown" is a legitimate value here.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <h2>How the site is funded</h2>
  <p style="max-width: var(--measure); color: var(--text-muted);">
    Advertising. Ads never influence what is published, which models are recommended, or the order of
    any list; nothing on this site is a paid placement. If that ever changes, the page it changes on
    will say so where the content is.
  </p>

  <h2>Corrections</h2>
  <p style="max-width: var(--measure); color: var(--text-muted);">
    If a number here is wrong, we want to know — a wrong price is worse than no price. Email
    <a href="mailto:privacy@hunteralphahub.com">privacy@hunteralphahub.com</a> with the URL and what we
    got wrong, and we will fix the page and note the date it changed.
  </p>

  <p class="hero-actions">
    <a class="btn primary" href="/contact">Contact us →</a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/privacy">Privacy policy</a>
    <a class="btn ghost" href="/terms">Terms of service</a>
  </p>
</System>
